// Checked in on purpose. Copy this file to `Config/Secrets.xcconfig`
// (gitignored) and fill in the real values from the Supabase project — the
// SAME project usephi.io uses. Ask Spitz for them; don't mint new ones.
//
// Both keys are consumed by Info.plist build-setting substitution
// ($(SUPABASE_URL) / $(SUPABASE_ANON_KEY)) and read back at runtime by
// Services/SupabaseClient.swift.
//
// XCCONFIG GOTCHA: `//` starts a comment in xcconfig, so the URL scheme's
// double slash must be broken with an empty `$()` expansion or everything
// after `https:` is silently dropped. Pattern: https:/$()/your-ref.supabase.co
//
// The anon key is DESIGNED to be embedded in client apps — RLS, not key
// secrecy, is the access-control boundary. The service-role key must NEVER
// appear here, in this repo, or in any mirror of it.
SUPABASE_URL = https:/$()/YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = your-anon-public-key
